;; ADR-2607182410: named-capability counterpart of capability-policy.edn --
;; capability-named.kotoba writes `(cap-call :identity/sign value)` instead
;; of a magic integer.
;;
;; Since 2026-09-01 the POLICY may be written in the same names
;; (kotoba.compiler.capability-names): `:identity/sign` is canonicalised to
;; its wire id 1 at decode, before admission and before provenance, so this
;; file and `{:allow #{[:cap/call 1]}}` are the same policy -- same
;; `:policy-sha256`, same artifact, byte for byte. `admission.cljc` still
;; never sees a keyword; it decides on the resolved [:cap/call 1] effect.
{:allow #{[:cap/call :identity/sign]}}
